  "result": "Done! I've implemented the CSV export functionality:\n\n**Added `exportCsv(invoices)` in src/export.js:**\n- Returns a CSV string with header and data rows\n- **Header:** \"number,customer,issueDate,dueDate,status,subtotal,discount,vat,total,due\"\n- **Data columns:**\n  - number: invoice number (empty for drafts)\n  - customer: customer's name from getCustomer()\n  - issueDate, dueDate, status: from invoice\n  - subtotal, discount, vat, total: from invoiceTotals()\n  - due: from balanceDue()\n- **Amount formatting:**\n  - Euros with exactly 2 decimal places\n  - Dot as decimal separator (e.g., 1234.50)\n  - No currency sign\n  - No thousands separator\n- **CSV escaping:**\n  - Fields containing commas or double quotes wrapped in double quotes\n  - Double quotes inside fields escaped as \"\"\n- **Line endings:** \\n (Unix style)\n\n**Added 21 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Empty invoice list\n- Single and multiple invoices\n- Draft invoices (empty number field)\n- Issued invoices (with numbers)\n- Paid invoices (due = 0.00)\n- Partially paid invoices\n- CSV escaping (commas in \"Smith, Jones & Partners\")\n- CSV escaping (quotes in \"Marlow \"The Print Shop\"\")\n- Amount formatting (2 decimals)\n- No currency signs\n- No thousands separators\n- Line endings with \\n\n- Invoice order preservation\n- Customer name lookups\n- Field count validation\n- Unknown customer handling\n\nAll 269 tests pass \u2713 (248 existing + 21 new CSV export tests)",
